# Environment of the Node adapter in the container image (docs/self-hosting.md). The image already sets these values;
# this file is for compose or `docker run --env-file` when one of them has to change.
# TLS ends at the reverse proxy in front of the container.
SELF_HOSTED=1
# All clients share one address behind the proxy: the per-address page limit would block everyone.
RATE_LIMIT_PER_MIN=0
# CLIENT_IP_HEADER is unset: the address is the socket's. Behind a proxy that sets a header, name it here and set
# TRUSTED_PROXIES to the number of proxies in front of the container.
# CLIENT_IP_HEADER=X-Forwarded-For
# TRUSTED_PROXIES=1
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://retro.example.org
